{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1545424-w5-and-the-war-of-rage","id":1545424,"title":"W5 and the War of Rage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-05T18:57:03-08:00","id":1545424,"title":"W5 and the War of Rage","content":"So, it's no secret that Garou got vast amounts of material torn from their game so that they would fit into a V5 campaign. Among those casualties are:<br /> <br /> - Pack Tactics and Maneuvers<br /> - Most Powerful Gifts<br /> - Gift access for medium-grade powers (moved to elder-level)<br /> - Significant Pack Patron bonuses<br /> - Access to the Umbra<br /> - Moon Bridges, focusing on Attack Moon Bridges (see the Rite of Luna's Spear from most editions of legacy material)<br /> - Crinos utility and endurance<br /> - Large groups of Garou unable to do anything because they'll just frenzy and tear each other apart before too long.<br /> - Rage extra actions (technically a Gift, but...)<br /> - Spirit of the Fray no longer auto-wins initiative, just patches back in Rage extra actions.<br /> <br /> Given this body of reduced capability, I posit that in so thoroughly clipping the wings of the Garou, they are no longer capable of having perpetrated the War of Rage in any way that would give them a significant advantage. They no longer have the action economy advantage against large, singular targets (wtf, I know), meaning that singular Gurahl would probably wipe the floor with them; Silver Claws takes forever to get, so they don't have that advantage against other werebeasts; there's no way to bypass caern defenses, so offense against the other sacred sites would always be at a distinct disadvantage; Garou might not have been able to step sideways more easily than other changers. And finally, there is no synergy for acting as a pack; in fact, this puts them at a horrible disadvantage against foes, because of the likelihood that they all collectively blow up and either tear each other apart or lose the wolf.<br /> <br /> W5 had aims behind it that were so obsessed with de-powering the Garou, that they did not even bother to consider the setting cohesiveness in this factor. Without the massive advantages that they had in prior material, there's no reason to believe in the slightest that the Garou managed to do any more than any other changer, and if they're written as having utterly scourged the other changers like in the old version, it'll be in the form of so many empty words without anything of substance to back it up.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T21:16:30-08:00","id":1545433,"title":"","content":"I think the obvious answer is just to say that the other Fera are going to get nerfed too. Why wouldn't the Gurahl's gifts and ability to gain health levels be nerfed if the Garou are? And even if some of the Garou's edges are just gone, the fact that they're more social means they'll still have at least one edge over single combatants with about the same capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T21:30:43-08:00","id":1545436,"title":"","content":"It's impossible for the Garou to be more social and organized - they flip out extra hard when they work together and ruin every plan that they have, remember? Everything handed to them is ashes and shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T21:53:17-08:00","id":1545438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1545424-w5-and-the-war-of-rage?p=1545433#post1545433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the obvious answer is just to say that the other Fera are going to get nerfed too. Why wouldn't the Gurahl's gifts and ability to gain health levels be nerfed if the Garou are? And even if some of the Garou's edges are just gone, the fact that they're more social means they'll still have at least one edge over single combatants with about the same capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honstly I won't be suprised if gaia was behind the depowering of the garou as some punishment for some vague transgressions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T22:33:00-08:00","id":1545439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1545424-w5-and-the-war-of-rage?p=1545438#post1545438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honstly I won't be suprised if gaia was behind the depowering of the garou as some punishment for some vague transgressions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not been how the setting worked (the consequences are the punishment), but this is the hellscape of VV5, so it wouldn't surprise me, either, because the guy on top Does Not Get It and also unfortunately Does Not Care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T23:30:18-08:00","id":1545443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1545424-w5-and-the-war-of-rage?p=1545439#post1545439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not been how the setting worked (the consequences are the punishment), but this is the hellscape of VV5, so it wouldn't surprise me, either, because the guy on top Does Not Get It and also unfortunately Does Not Care.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes and that why if I'm in charge of WtA I would just retcon the whole edition taking place in Beta for the Pentex MMO and the first advebture would be the PCs pulling a Matrix and rescuing the garou souls that power the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T05:41:32-08:00","id":1545458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1545424-w5-and-the-war-of-rage?p=1545443#post1545443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes and that why if I'm in charge of WtA I would just retcon the whole edition taking place in Beta for the Pentex MMO and the first advebture would be the PCs pulling a Matrix and rescuing the garou souls that power the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard you the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T05:57:31-08:00","id":1545460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1545424-w5-and-the-war-of-rage#post1545424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it's no secret that Garou got vast amounts of material torn from their game so that they would fit into a V5 campaign. Among those casualties are:<br /> <br /> - Pack Tactics and Maneuvers<br /> - Most Powerful Gifts<br /> - Gift access for medium-grade powers (moved to elder-level)<br /> - Significant Pack Patron bonuses<br /> - Access to the Umbra<br /> - Moon Bridges, focusing on Attack Moon Bridges (see the Rite of Luna's Spear from most editions of legacy material)<br /> - Crinos utility and endurance<br /> - Large groups of Garou unable to do anything because they'll just frenzy and tear each other apart before too long.<br /> - Rage extra actions (technically a Gift, but...)<br /> - Spirit of the Fray no longer auto-wins initiative, just patches back in Rage extra actions.<br /> <br /> Given this body of reduced capability, I posit that in so thoroughly clipping the wings of the Garou, they are no longer capable of having perpetrated the War of Rage in any way that would give them a significant advantage. They no longer have the action economy advantage against large, singular targets (wtf, I know), meaning that singular Gurahl would probably wipe the floor with them; Silver Claws takes forever to get, so they don't have that advantage against other werebeasts; there's no way to bypass caern defenses, so offense against the other sacred sites would always be at a distinct disadvantage; Garou might not have been able to step sideways more easily than other changers. And finally, there is no synergy for acting as a pack; in fact, this puts them at a horrible disadvantage against foes, because of the likelihood that they all collectively blow up and either tear each other apart or lose the wolf.<br /> <br /> W5 had aims behind it that were so obsessed with de-powering the Garou, that they did not even bother to consider the setting cohesiveness in this factor. Without the massive advantages that they had in prior material, there's no reason to believe in the slightest that the Garou managed to do any more than any other changer, and if they're written as having utterly scourged the other changers like in the old version, it'll be in the form of so many empty words without anything of substance to back it up.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have an alternative hypothesis: the war of rage is just a day when all the fera meet in the same place, and because of how rage works now, they just frenzy together and kill each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T07:25:00-08:00","id":1545464,"title":"","content":"The War of Rage in particular is one element that's very emblematic of how W5 handles its &quot;lore&quot;.<br /> <br /> First, you start in the Corebook with this on pg 284:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou wish they knew, for it might make interacting with these other shapechangers less volatile. Sometimes, other shifters indicate that some long-ago grudge shaped the relationship the Garou have with them today \u2014 which would certainly be in keeping with today\u2019s Garou bearing the responsibility of past times of legend. </div> </div> </div>So there you have your &quot;Who knows&quot;-approach that's so typical for the W5 corebook. The War of Rage happened but the Garou <i>somehow</i> have completely forgotten that it has happened. But the premise is &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; and so you have some wriggle-room here to make this work. Maybe it's very different compared to how it was handled in the legacy-editions. It would take a bit of work and it feels a bit lazy for the official stance to just summarize the whole thing with &quot;Who knows what happened and who did what?&quot;. And yet things in W5 are very confounding in that regard. The premise says &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; and the reason you can consider this approach a failure is that strangely whenever W5 has to fill out this barren setting where everything was destroyed... it always goes back to the legacy-editions.<br /> <br /> Take the Gurahl/Bear-Shifters. Here's what it says in Shattered Nation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bear-shifters often have a knack for healing, and legend states that Bear herself gave them a Rite that resurrects the dead. It was this, the older ones say, that the shifters of the world craved and slaughtered them to near extinction for. Whether this Rite exists or is an exaggeration of their medical prowess is a mystery.\u200b </div> </div> </div>The approach is still &quot;It's a mystery. Who knows what's true?&quot;. But in the same way, the first quote was just pointing at the War of Rage from previous editions, the Bear-Shifter description points at the Gurahl from previous editions. Where's the &quot;re-imagination&quot;-part in any of this? Simply erasing most of the details of legacy-lore and instead adding a heavy dose of &quot;Who knows if it's true...&quot; doesn't add anything of value. You're not presenting something new doing it like this, you're just presenting the old stuff again in a worse way!<br /> <br /> And that's the central problem of W5: The WtA-premise has been thrown under the bus. Garou Nation gone, Gaia dead/dying, Age of Apocalypse... and what did this edition get in return? Nothing. Well, aside from more punishing mechanics and a hardcoded doom-spiral. I mean, there has been criticism of WtA and the game has its problems. But I've never heard of anybody suggesting that what this game needed was a doom-spiral. And that also brings me back to another point for why I don't like the &quot;Garou as activist&quot;. If you really believe &quot;Garou are a good insert for climate-activism&quot;, then how do you square that with putting them in a game with a mechanic that dooms PCs to lose? What the hell is that supposed to say about environmental activism? Not even V5 is that nihilistic. It's about the struggle with Humanity but V5 isn't saying that every vampire is doomed to reach Humanity 0 at some point - but W5 is saying exactly that sort of thing about Garou with Harano and Hauglosk.<br /> <br /> Where it gets even more absurd os that W5 has to fill out the world every time you're tasking people with writing supplements like Shattered Nation. If you wanna stick to the whole &quot;Who knows&quot;-thing... well, there's only so many times you can just pick elements in the setting and tell the reader that nobody knows anything about this. And so instead, slowly but surely we probably will just get more regurgitated legacy-lore. Sometimes it's truly odd like when they brought back Albrecht to present him as a cranky, self-important old man and other times it's just a copy-paste. What has Shattered Nation to say about Moots? Well, do you have the W20 corebook? Then you already know everything there is to know. Rather than introducing something new or present an old concept in a changed form... nope, it's just the same-old thing from the previous editions. Not just that, we already know of a couple of times where W5 writers have actually just copy-pasted stuff from the W20 corebook (without crediting any of the W20 writers of course or mentioning that they have done this). (And on that note, we also know that Paradox/Renegade still pilfer the Hunters Entertainment W5 draft for ideas without crediting those writers.)<br /> <br /> And whenever they're going to delve deeper into the relationship between the shifters and the Garou, it's probably gonna be that mix of copy-pasting legacy-lore and some odd decisions to portray an old thing in a negative light to explain why everything sucks now in the W5-seting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T03:08:34-08:00","id":1545681,"title":"","content":"I mean, depending on when you plonk the War of Rage it could even justify the lack of knowledge Garou seem to have. You'd need to establish what the Garou have done since then, although there's an arguably interesting take of it having happened within living memory that W5 could have used.<br /> <br /> Hell you could even have the War of Rage be the reason the Nation fell, or a cycle of hubris where the Garou grow in strength, decide to take the other shifters' jobs, and get absolutely mullered and lose their culture and lore because of how few are left.<br /> <br /> But W5 being W5 they'll probably go for the least interesting option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T16:11:47-08:00","id":1545715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b