27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T15:13:16-08:00","id":1546093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1545424-w5-and-the-war-of-rage?p=1546081#post1546081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are you referring to? I can think of a couple of things you could be asking about but I'm not sure what exactly... &quot;Depowering the Garou to make it easier&quot; - easier than what? Are we talking editions or changes within W5...? For example.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the OP:<br /> <br /> <i>So, it's no secret that Garou got vast amounts of material torn from their game so that they would fit into a V5 campaign. Among those casualties are:<br /> <br /> - Pack Tactics and Maneuvers<br /> - Most Powerful Gifts<br /> - Gift access for medium-grade powers (moved to elder-level)<br /> - Significant Pack Patron bonuses<br /> - Access to the Umbra<br /> - Moon Bridges, focusing on Attack Moon Bridges (see the Rite of Luna's Spear from most editions of legacy material)<br /> - Crinos utility and endurance<br /> - Large groups of Garou unable to do anything because they'll just frenzy and tear each other apart before too long.<br /> - Rage extra actions (technically a Gift, but...)<br /> - Spirit of the Fray no longer auto-wins initiative, just patches back in Rage extra actions.<br /> </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https:/